From c5cdcb23af37bf1b6a44dbbb38b88c521d2f552c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 08:00:56 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] slimbus: qcom-ngd-ctrl: propagate resume errors before
 registration

Runtime resume records a failed power-up state but always returns success.
Controller enable also ignores both the direct callback and PM framework
resume results. An initial QMI, DMA setup or capability exchange failure
can therefore expose a controller and consume its bootstrap PM reference
before hardware startup has succeeded. Registered wake failures are hidden
from their callers too.

Return the power-up error from runtime resume and check both resume paths
before registration. Unwind the new QMI client only for an unregistered
controller, retaining its bootstrap reference for retry or removal. A
failed wake of an already registered controller retains its registration
and existing client. Accept nonnegative PM framework success, including
its positive already-active result. Prepared DMA resources retain their
existing ownership for retry and normal teardown.

A host model composes 15 exact driver, core and PM callback bodies against
logical DMA, MMIO, QMI, completion and PM services. Each of two PM profiles
executes 626 cases: current PM passes 13284 checks after 2435 parent
failures; the cached 6.18.63 PM callback passes 12708 after 2652 failures.
The latter explicitly verifies hard-error latching and blocked retry; it
does not qualify an LTS backport or its recovery. Twelve independent
regression controls are rejected. Native ARM/ARM64 NGD/core objects build
with LLVM21, W=1 and strict callback diagnostics without warnings/errors.

Master-work and external-transfer quiescence, full failed-start recovery,
late QMI service handling and initial bootstrap remain separate work.
No real DMA, DMA callbacks, firmware, audio or phone operations ran. Codex
generated the fix, tests and changelog; human review and DCO are pending.

Fixes: 917809e2280b ("slimbus: ngd: Add qcom SLIMBus NGD driver")
Fixes: 94fe5f2b45c4 ("silmbus: ngd: register controller after power up.")
---
 drivers/slimbus/qcom-ngd-ctrl.c | 11 ++++++++---
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/slimbus/qcom-ngd-ctrl.c b/drivers/slimbus/qcom-ngd-ctrl.c
index 867a9f94f..c6a5296d1 100644
--- a/drivers/slimbus/qcom-ngd-ctrl.c
+++ b/drivers/slimbus/qcom-ngd-ctrl.c
@@ -1426,7 +1426,7 @@ static int qcom_slim_ngd_runtime_resume(struct device *dev)
 		ctrl->state = QCOM_SLIM_NGD_CTRL_AWAKE;
 	}
 
-	return 0;
+	return ret;
 }
 
 static int qcom_slim_ngd_enable(struct qcom_slim_ngd_ctrl *ctrl, bool enable)
@@ -1446,9 +1446,14 @@ static int qcom_slim_ngd_enable(struct qcom_slim_ngd_ctrl *ctrl, bool enable)
 		complete(&ctrl->qmi.qmi_comp);
 		if (!pm_runtime_enabled(ctrl->ctrl.dev) ||
 			 !pm_runtime_suspended(ctrl->ctrl.dev))
-			qcom_slim_ngd_runtime_resume(ctrl->ctrl.dev);
+			ret = qcom_slim_ngd_runtime_resume(ctrl->ctrl.dev);
 		else
-			pm_runtime_resume(ctrl->ctrl.dev);
+			ret = pm_runtime_resume(ctrl->ctrl.dev);
+		if (ret < 0) {
+			if (!ctrl->registered)
+				qcom_slim_qmi_exit(ctrl);
+			return ret;
+		}
 
 		if (ctrl->registered)
 			return 0;
